ECE1387 A1 - FPGA maze router (Sara Sehgal)

build
-----
  make

(needs gtk3, same as the ezgl example. builds ./router)

run
---
run it from this folder (it loads main.ui from here):

  ./router circuits/cct1

that routes cct1 w the W from the file and opens the graphics window.
W + number of segments used are printed in the terminal n shown in the status bar.

options (can combine them):
  -minw    find the smallest W that routes (tries W = 1, 2, 3, ...)
  -fc      part 4: odd/even connection block
  -fs4     part 5: Fs = 4 switch block
  -nogfx   just print the result, no window

examples:
  ./router circuits/cct2
  ./router circuits/cct3 -minw
  ./router circuits/cct4 -minw -fc
  ./router circuits/cct4 -minw -fs4 -nogfx

files
-----
  router.cpp       the router (everything is in this one file)
  Makefile
  main.ui, ezgl/   ezgl graphics lib (from the course page)
  circuits/        test circuits cct1 - cct4
  A1_report.pdf    report
